REQUIRES: libxml2
UNSUPPORTED: system-windows

Write the merged manifest to the RT_MANIFEST resource of a PE image.
RUN: yaml2obj %p/Inputs/pe.yaml -o %t.exe
RUN: llvm-mt /manifest %p/Inputs/test_manifest.manifest /manifest %p/Inputs/additional.manifest /outputresource:%t.exe
RUN: llvm-readobj --coff-resources %t.exe | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RESOURCES
RUN: llvm-mt /inputresource:%t.exe /out:%t.manifest
RUN: llvm-mt /manifest %p/Inputs/test_manifest.manifest /manifest %p/Inputs/additional.manifest /out:%t.expected.manifest
RUN: diff %t.expected.manifest %t.manifest

RESOURCES:      Type: MANIFEST (ID 24) [
RESOURCES:        Name: (ID 1) [
RESOURCES:          Language: (ID 0) [

The resource ID defaults to 1 and can be given with or without a '#'. Existing
resources are replaced.
RUN: llvm-mt /manifest %p/Inputs/additional.manifest "/outputresource:%t.exe;#1"
RUN: llvm-mt /manifest %p/Inputs/additional.manifest "/outputresource:%t.exe;2"
RUN: llvm-readobj --coff-resources %t.exe | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RESOURCES2
RUN: llvm-mt "/inputresource:%t.exe;#1" /out:%t.1.manifest
RUN: llvm-mt "/inputresource:%t.exe;#2" /out:%t.2.manifest
RUN: llvm-mt /manifest %p/Inputs/additional.manifest /out:%t.expected2.manifest
RUN: diff %t.expected2.manifest %t.1.manifest
RUN: diff %t.expected2.manifest %t.2.manifest

RESOURCES2:      Type: MANIFEST (ID 24) [
RESOURCES2:        Name: (ID 1) [
RESOURCES2:          Language: (ID 0) [
RESOURCES2:        Name: (ID 2) [
RESOURCES2:          Language: (ID 0) [

The manifest can be written to a file and a resource at the same time.
RUN: llvm-mt /manifest %p/Inputs/test_manifest.manifest /out:%t.3.manifest /outputresource:%t.exe
RUN: llvm-mt /inputresource:%t.exe /out:%t.4.manifest
RUN: diff %t.3.manifest %t.4.manifest

With /notify_update, the exit code indicates whether the resource changed.
RUN: not llvm-mt /manifest %p/Inputs/additional.manifest /outputresource:%t.exe /notify_update
RUN: llvm-mt /manifest %p/Inputs/additional.manifest /outputresource:%t.exe /notify_update

Errors.
RUN: not llvm-mt /manifest %p/Inputs/test_manifest.manifest /outputresource:%p/Inputs/test_manifest.manifest 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NOT-OBJECT
NOT-OBJECT: llvm-mt: error: '{{.*}}test_manifest.manifest': The file was not recognized as a valid object file

RUN: not llvm-mt /manifest %p/Inputs/test_manifest.manifest "/outputresource:%t.exe;#" 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=INVALID-ID
INVALID-ID: llvm-mt: error: invalid resource ID in '{{.*}}.exe;#'
